    "examples": [
      {
        "question_text": "(a) Write $61\\div8=7$ remainder $5$ as a multiplication-and-addition equation.\n(b) Write the division by $6$ represented by $50=6\\times8+2$.",
        "solution_text": "(a) $61=8\\times7+5=56+5$.\n(b) $50\\div6=8$ remainder $2$, since $6\\times8+2=50$.\nBoth remainders are less than their divisors."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "(a) A division has divisor $7$, quotient $9$ and remainder $4$. Find the dividend.\n(b) A student writes $67\\div7=8$ remainder $11$. Check and repair this claim.",
        "solution_text": "(a) Dividend $=7\\times9+4=63+4=67$.\n(b) $7\\times8+11=56+11=67$, but $11$ is not less than $7$.\nAnother group can be made: $11=7+4$.\nThe correct statement is $67\\div7=9$ remainder $4$."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "(a) Find $q$ in $94=8\\times q+6$, then state the division by $8$.\n(b) Complete $73=9\\times8+r$.",
        "solution_text": "(a) $94-6=88$.\n$q=88\\div8=11$.\n$94\\div8=11$ remainder $6$.\nCheck: $8\\times11+6=94$, and $6<8$.\n(b) $9\\times8=72$.\n$r=73-72=1$.\nCheck: $9\\times8+1=73$, and $1<9$."
      }
    ],
